:[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T15:18:45-07:00","id":1122818,"title":"","content":"By far the Sluagh. Eshu is a distant second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T17:27:40-07:00","id":1122855,"title":"","content":"Boggins, probably. Also Pooka, but I use them so differently than seems to be the norm, I'm not sure they'd count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T17:32:44-07:00","id":1122857,"title":"","content":"Sidhes.<br /> <br /> But i like Merfolk too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T17:45:37-07:00","id":1122860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122473-what-is-your-favorite-kith?p=1122855#post1122855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boggins, probably. Also Pooka, but I use them so differently than seems to be the norm, I'm not sure they'd count.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you use the Pooka?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T08:13:53-07:00","id":1123024,"title":"","content":"Pooka! Nockers and Eshu are good too. I'm really hoping for a chance to play a Korred or a Wolpertinger sometime <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:39:54-07:00","id":1123154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122473-what-is-your-favorite-kith?p=1123024#post1123024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pooka! Nockers and Eshu are good too. I'm really hoping for a chance to play a Korred or a Wolpertinger sometime <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cream pies in a spring loaded box sends a strong, political message between houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:52:00-07:00","id":1123160,"title":"","content":"If anyone could like them, I would choose Redcap, but alas. Second best would have to be Sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T14:02:03-07:00","id":1123168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkeydjie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122473-what-is-your-favorite-kith?p=1123160#post1123160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anyone could like them, I would choose Redcap, but alas. Second best would have to be Sidhe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've known a few people with Redcap as their favourite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:05:38-07:00","id":1123189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122473-what-is-your-favorite-kith?p=1122860#post1122860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you use the Pooka?</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on them has always been that they're creatures of Wisdom, in the sense that they are supposed to teach lessons through the Trickster methods of misdirection, subterfuge and cunning. They aren't in any way things of innocence or frivolity, unless such a pose advances some hidden agenda. And they most certainly are not clowns. (The &quot;who farted?&quot; bit in the Kithbook made me fling the book across the room in annoyance and disgust when I first read it.) And sometimes, especially in the case of the Unseelie, those lessons can be harsh ones. They are Confidants because they instinctively know what makes others tick; they Shapechange into animal forms because such creatures are deeply intertwined with the stories and legends of Tricksters. They will not tell the full truth because doing so would fail to teach others the lessons they need to learn, as they need to be able to figure things out for themselves without you explaining it to them. If you'd asked me to come up with a Pooka signature character for the game, it would've been Aunt Nancy, the elder Afro-Carribean charismatic and manipulative voodoo priestess who is constantly weaving endless webs within webs of intrigue, her animal form being a spider (obviously paying homage to Anansi, the West African spider trickster). Probably as an Unseelie member of House Eiluned, if she was going to be a noble.<br /> I'm also really really picky about how the Pooka Frailty should be portrayed. Simple and childish falsehoods are, pardon the phrase, banal as all hell. Too me, every Pooka should have a very personalized manifestation of their Frailty, and it should tie into her character concept. The Seelie White Swan Maid of the Noblity who lives a secret double life as an Unseelie Black Swan Knight of the Commoner revolution (or vice versa). The loud and outspoken Junkyard Dog whose bark is much worse than his bite, his blustery bravado quickly evaporating if actually challenged. The cute and perky teenaged Beach Bunny (and yes, I have a weakness for bad animal puns) who has all the guys wrapped around her little finger with the right mix of fake smiles and empty flirtation. That sort of thing. <br /> <br /> (And since the Pooka are creatures of Wisdom, their dark cousins, the Beasties, are things of Madness. And if a Pooka were to fall into service of banality - or Apathy as I prefer to use it - he'd end up an embodiment of Ignorance.)<br /> <br /> So like I said, I like the Kith quite a bit, but my take on them has always been a bit askew from the norm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:13:34-07:00","id":1123194,"title":"","content":"Ah, I don't handle any kith as rigidly as that. It certainly fits well within my concept of the kith (as do clowns, as does someone like the Joker).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T16:04:54-07:00","id":1123215,"title":"","content":"It's less an issue of rigidity as it is a multi decade reaction to what people used to call FishMalks. I've no idea where said term originated, but it originally referred to Vampire players who would play Malkavians as what were essentially obnoxious pests whose only purpose was to annoy everyone with their childish antics for the player's amusement, using their &quot;insanity&quot; as justification for this stupidity. A text book example of this is from a LARP in which three Malkavian players walked about arm in arm and would literally stand in people's way while proclaiming &quot;we're a hedge!&quot; That is a true story. Werewolf never had this problem, Mage's Marauders were never really presented as player character options, and total lack of focus on Legions in Wraith meant that no one ever latched on to the &quot;those who died of madness&quot; group that way. But with the Pooka, you had a doubling down on it. I again point to the &quot;who farted?&quot; bit from the Kith book. I find that sort of thing tiresome on an almost spiritual level. And I say this as some one who still loves the Three Stooges, Mel Brooks movies, and Three's Company. If you're going to play a Pooka, all I ask is that, for pity's sake, please be <b><i>clever</i></b> about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T16:55:34-07:00","id":1123231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122473-what-is-your-favorite-kith?p=1123215#post1123215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's less an issue of rigidity as it is a multi decade reaction to what people used to call FishMalks. I've no idea where said term originated</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This has led to the term &quot;Fishmalks&quot; in the community, after one particularly infamous Malkavian PC and art where one was kissing a fish.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Chaotic_Stupid\" target=\"_blank\">Chaotic Stupid Alignment</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-31-2017, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T14:21:43-07:00","id":1123631,"title":"","content":"It's either the Sluagh or the Goblins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Give before you take, or I'll hit you with a rake&quot; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">~ Socrates</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5638-kaizer-gibby","name":"Kaizer Gibby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5638_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T14:34:33-07:00","id":1123638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122473-what-is-your-favorite-kith?p=1123168#post1123168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've known a few people with Redcap as their favourite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to their flaw <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T14:52:42-07:00","id":1123645,"title":"","content":"My favourite Thallain are the Bogarts, because I think they make the best villains. Goblins are pretty fun too though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T09:29:46-07:00","id":1125255,"title":"","content":"If mindset is the deciding issue, then Eshu are most preferred and Satyrs are second best. If powers are the gauge, then Trolls, Redcaps, and Autumn Sidhe are the ones I really fancy in this rough order of preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 08-05-2017, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T12:48:06-07:00","id":1125314,"title":"","content":"Pooka and autumn sidhe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T16:37:15-07:00","id":1126101,"title":"","content":"When I first read the books (not too long ago, actually), I would say Trolls, Satyrs, and Sidhe (not necessarily in this order, and possibly Autumn Sidhe specifically depending on my read of C20?). I also like Boggans (mad respect for them) and Eshu, although they feel more like NPCs to me a bit (Boggans generally, and Eshu if the PC group is involved in a chronicle involving a single location).<br /> <br /> I also enjoy House Scathach, but I promise I'm not someone interested in having a special snowflake/murderhobo character. I initially enjoyed learning about them being the only House to stay behind (this was before C20), and their repudiation of Title/nobility to some extent combined with staying behind for the sake of the greater good (notably ending the Ascension War more quickly and saving Kithain lives, fighting against the potentially awful fate of the Dreaming, fighting against fate for the greater good instead of resigning to it, etc.) is appealing. My one counterpoint to them would be that ignoring politics might actually be a mistake for Scathach's overall goals. The right political leadership is worth a great many assassinations, killing enemies of the Dreaming, or rescuing individual kithain here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T14:33:59-07:00","id":1126452,"title":"","content":"Its kind of a toss up between Rock Giants and Selkies....for completely different reasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T16:06:01-07:00","id":1126492,"title":"","content":"I pretty much love all the Kiths but the top two would likely be Arcadian Sidhe, especially Houses Eilil, Ailuned and Balor, and the Sluagh. Third spot is extremely difficult to choose but it would be a fight between Pooka, Redcaps and Nockers. The only Kiths I dont particularly like would be the Selkies and Boggans.<br /> <br /> Of the Adhene my favorite two would be the Acheri and the Moirae with Keremet taking the third place.<br /> <br /> My favorite Thallain pre-C20 would have been the Bogies, Goblins and the Merrow. Now I'm yet unsure if Sevartal would take the top place, since I still have issues organizing my mind on what is their unique thematic space compared to the Balor as I feel they are best suited for things I previously used Balor for, but they have a good chance to do so. Likewise the Ghasts are likely going to cut their place quite high on my list even though they do have a rather impactful Frailty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T02:29:35-07:00","id":1126631,"title":"","content":"Trolls followed by pooka and sluagh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13369-chameleon","name":"Chameleon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13369_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T16:50:35-07:00","id":1126888,"title":"","content":"As I think about this more if I were to start today in a game as a player I would pick an Autumn sidhe, mostly because it's a perspective I haven't explored much in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T08:31:28-07:00","id":1133024,"title":"","content":"Pookas<br /> Redcaps<br /> Sluagh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T18:30:25-07:00","id":1134308,"title":"","content":"Sidhe and Pookas are what I play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T10:55:55-07:00","id":1134878,"title":"","content":"Troll, far and away above any other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T20:42:45-07:00","id":1135049,"title":"","content":"Troll, Sluagh, Redcap, Eshu, Ghille Dhu. <br /> <br /> Dishonorable mention for playing Sidhe and Beasties. I find Unseelie Sidhe to be generally more interesting than Seelie, and I enjoy Beasties overall moreso than Pooka.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T13:19:39-07:00","id":1136343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122473-what-is-your-favorite-kith?p=1135049#post1135049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find Unseelie Sidhe to be generally more interesting than Seelie, and I enjoy Beasties overall moreso than Pooka.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always sort of saw Beasties as akin to playing one of the monsters in Call of Cthulhu, which can be rather fun, I think. <br /> <br /> As for Seelie Sidhe, I always figured if I ever played one again - unlikely, but anything can happen - he'd either be a member of House Dougal who is literally King of the Nerds, or one of House Gwydion whose some sort of paragon of 1920s Marcus Garvey-style proto-Fascism (real Fascism, not what most people mean when they use the term) and W.E.B. DeBois's &quot;Talented Tenth&quot; elitism. Probably the Dougal one, since it's more light hearted. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T00:12:04-07:00","id":1137934,"title":"","content":"I absolutely LOVE Adhene. Every single one of them, but especially Keremeth and Firbolg. Never played. But love them.<br /> <br /> I've played Houses Eiluned and Gwydion of Sidhe and my take on them, that while they were actively Seelie, their &quot;heroic&quot; and &quot;good natured&quot; decisions were hugely influenced by constant reminder their &quot;darker&quot; Unseelies sides and even destructive Seelie impulses, to one degree or another. In my case it was Knight/Pandora and Knight/Beast, respectively.<br /> I had good understanding of how my character would act in accord with both of their Legacies and what could make them switch Legacies. (By the way, cool idea for a Cantrip...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T09:56:41-07:00","id":1138043,"title":"","content":"Are we limited just to Kithain? If so, I'm fond of selkies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T19:07:04-07:00","id":1138178,"title":"","content":"KIths that aren't Eshu. This is mostly because their Kithbook failled the Chuptest hard...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T19:13:38-07:00","id":1138470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122473-what-is-your-favorite-kith?p=1136343#post1136343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always sort of saw Beasties as akin to playing one of the monsters in Call of Cthulhu, which can be rather fun, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What's with this maneuver that you wrote on your character sheet, let's see... here? '<a href=\"https://darkestdungeon.gamepedia.com/Cultist_Priest\" target=\"_blank\">The Finger</a>'? Does that do what I think it does?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It is a dread strike that puts down both the body and spirit!&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T21:56:47-07:00","id":1138497,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Sidhe are the most fleshed out and Nockers are always cool, also Boggan sorcerers have their moments, but my favorite kiths are always home-brewed. Dragons, Djinn, Gargoyles are my favorite although the site with dragons is gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T13:05:22-07:00","id":1138683,"title":"","content":"Way back in 1st edition days, like '94 or '95, I had an idea for Dragon: The Somethingorother, in which all the clan-breeds were descended from mythological dragons - Tiamat, Vritra, Fafnir, Kukulkan, Kanghui, etc. - and were meant to be heralds of the end times or something. I wish I still had a copy, though in hindsight I'm sure it was painfully awful.<br /> <br /> I'm still a little disappointed that Land of 8 Million Dreams didn't have a kith based on the legends of noble families descended from dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T15:25:41-07:00","id":1138715,"title":"","content":"It gauls me how many amazing homebrew kiths have disappeared over the years as their websites disappeared. There were some REALLY good ones and I wish I remembered all of their websites names so I can look them up on WebArchive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T20:50:34-07:00","id":1138791,"title":"","content":"I imagine we will get Drake and Djinn in the PG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T01:33:40-07:00","id":1140737,"title":"","content":"Personally, I've always been partial to Satyrs; they tend to be the 'live free or die, Sidhe suck' types, especially the one I'm playing currently. I've also had some fun with bat Pooka (people keep mistaking them for succubi...). Whatever I play, though, it always ends up being either generic Unseelie or flat-out Shadow Court. Hey, the Sidhe aren't going to feed themselves into that wood chipper...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16912-fjordymcfjord","name":"FjordyMcFjord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16912_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T01:25:14-07:00","id":1142071,"title":"","content":"Fir-bholg. Specifically, Fir-bholg as depicted in Mel Uran's style where they kind of have an antlered night-elfesque appearance.<br /> <br /> I do hope we get some supplements expanding on the Adhene, I found myself missing the Arts from the Denizens book (because making reality forget a person so hard that they're eventually drawn away as a phantom into the depths of the Dreaming is just cool).<br /> <br /> Some clarification on whether or not Breath of the Firchlis can affect the real world as it could originally would be very pleasant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T02:48:00-07:00","id":1142078,"title":"","content":"Selkies, Mer and Trolls for me.